<title>BELGIUM: EU SAYS CLEARS ICI-UNILEVER CHEMICALS TRANSACTION.</title>
<headline>EU SAYS CLEARS ICI-UNILEVER CHEMICALS TRANSACTION.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had cleared the purchase by British chemical company ICI plc of the speciality chemicals division of Unilever Plc.  </p>
<p>&quot;The operation does not give rise to competition concerns,&quot; the Commission said.</p>
<p>The three Unilever subsidiaries are National Starch, which makes industrial adhesives and starches for food and industrial use, Unichema, which makes fragrances, flavourings and food ingredients, and Crosfield, maker of alumina and silica-derived products, the Commission added.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
